The Deep was a great god that once threatened the world, and was slain in part through the help of [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]]. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] says the name appears in no record he has seen.

On [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] the Deep was a great source of power believed to reside at the planet's core. It powered some of the more taboo spells there, and its followers were the largest of [[Org/Althane/The Mysteries|the Mysteries]]. Ingesting its blood, deepblood, brings on [[Phenomena/Althane/Sanguis Depsics|Sanguis Depsics]].

It reached into [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]] from below. It broke the cognitive breakwater on the sixth floor, and where its touch fell people rose off the floor with mouths and eyes spilling yellow light, speaking together in one voice. They lunged at whatever came near and burst when they struck.

It pressed on the mind of [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]], trying to drag him down into slumber, and where he was wounded his flesh closed under a black silk. When Karkov was killed the Deep would not let him go: a portal opened and eight fungal tendrils, like the [[Phenomena/Althane/Mycelia|mycelium]] seen in [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Vyre, the Inverted City|Vyre]], reached out and dragged what was left of his body through. The Deep did not suffer anyone to walk up to the portal it opens.

Its seat was the City of Yellow on [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], a hill of yellow buildings ringed by cloud, with a lake of black water at the centre and a lighthouse standing in it. Fungal tendrils wrapped the lighthouse and found no way in. Above the city the Deep showed itself as a flat yellow faceplate with a single large red eye and two hands, too large to see whole, with tendrils of yellow floss reaching from its fingers. It held what was Karkov by those tendrils and worked him like a marionette over a great fungus organ at the top of the hill.

By the reckoning of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] it was the strongest of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]], though long weakened. It spoke as hundreds of overlapping voices that did not resolve into meaning, and beneath them an intent could be felt. It wanted into the lighthouse, and it offered to remake those who came to it into Thessians, the dynasty it called the Thessians of Yord, and to rebuild the empire that was taken from it.

[[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] destroyed it at the top of the City of Yellow. They broke its body apart and, before it could draw itself back together, [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] put a volley of thorny growth from his [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|duskwalker]] markings through the last of it; what was left burned to soot. The Thirteenth Realm's moon fell on the city in the same hour and wiped it off [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]].
